[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815112278,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81514632,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81515012,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815152744,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815155117,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815157421,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815159754,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815161915,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815164128,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815166254,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815168588,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81517879,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below 12 qubits (8 with mid-circuit measurement) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81518285,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches 12 qubits, or 8 with mid-circuit measurement (docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md, \"CPU against T4\") | IBM jobs; narrow replays, which the T4 speeds up by at most 3 times |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815185748,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815188225,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. An account without Persona identity verification gets a 4-core CPU machine for every TPU request; a verified account's request queues for a TPU, one batch session at a time (docs/notes/kaggle/tpu-research.md) | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815191197,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815193958,"data":"| A 15-qubit run (decision-gated) | the substrate an approved written case names: Kaggle T4 x2 or build host Aer, a GPU state wider than one T4 cache-blocked across both (`calibration_snapshot.blocking_options`; docs/notes/kaggle/gpu-runbook.md), or Tuna-17 through Quantum Inspire, whose `submit` refuses while another session's hardware job is live | any substrate the case does not name |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815196795,"data":"| IBM Heron r2 (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 16 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81520075,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81520318,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815205827,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815207962,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815210187,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815212337,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815218335,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815220787,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815222908,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815225213,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815227583,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices, the Aer device the entry\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815229883,"data":"   runs on (`entry_aer_device`) and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81523217,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack, built and proved by\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81523461,"data":"   `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`. `--fetch` downloads the seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815236982,"data":"   archives `RELEASES` pins and keeps each only if its sha256 matches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81523927,"data":"   `--install` installs sixteen of them with `pip install --no-deps`,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815241555,"data":"   applying `BUILD_RECIPES` (the cayley-dickson, SplitOct and pyquaternion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815243858,"data":"   PKGBUILD `prepare()` steps) and taking the Octonion-Sedenion wheel as\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815246157,"data":"   published, then installs `RUNTIME_PINS`: numpy-quaternion, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815248432,"data":"   seventeenth, as its pinned compiled wheel, and numba, sparse and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815250733,"data":"   anywidget. `--extract` binds all seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815253002,"data":"   installed distributions to their archives and regenerates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815255284,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json`; the kernel stops with exit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815257577,"data":"   code 3 unless those bytes equal the retained ones. The build host passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815259845,"data":"   the same test against its Arch packages, so a run that reaches its entry\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815262121,"data":"   used the same algebra code as the host. The file's `packages` field\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815264395,"data":"   records the versions `kernel_main.REPORTED_PACKAGES` names, nine of the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815266685,"data":"   seventeen algebra distributions; the byte comparison binds the rest.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815268964,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815271265,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815273475,"data":"4. The entry's stdout and stderr, written to `stdout.txt` and `stderr.txt`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815275768,"data":"   as the entry prints (`kernel_main.start_entry` sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815278378,"data":"   `PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1`), then its exit code and the repository files it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81528068,"data":"   changed, which the kernel copies under `repo/` after the entry exits.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815282959,"data":"   A session Kaggle ends at `--timeout` still returns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81528527,"data":"   `/kaggle/working/output` but never reaches that copy, so an entry that\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815287561,"data":"   may outlive its timeout writes its record to an absolute path under\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81529191,"data":"   `/kaggle/working/output` and rewrites it after every finished unit of\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815294362,"data":"   work, as `scripts/aer_gpu_probe.py` does per row.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815296622,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815298762,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815300968,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815303113,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815305361,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815307564,"data":"| qiskit | 2.6.0 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815309785,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815312232,"data":"| cuquantum-cu11 | 24.8.0 (brings custatevec-cu11 1.6.0.post1 and cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0; the libraries the cu11 Aer wheel links) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815317187,"data":"| cutensor-cu11 | 2.2.0 (the newest release inside cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0's `\u003e=2.0.1,\u003c3`) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815320133,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815322515,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815324962,"data":"| quaternionic, clifford, kingdon, galgebra, pyoctonion | 1.0.18, 1.5.1, 3.0.0, 0.6.0, 3.12 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815327343,"data":"| pyquaternion | 0.9.9 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe (writes the VERSION.txt the sdist omits) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815329705,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815332047,"data":"| hyprat | 0.2.0 | GitHub tag archive, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815334483,"data":"| Octonion-Sedenion | 1.0.0 | PyPI wheel (its only release form), sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815336817,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI compiled wheel at the pin; `--extract` binds its Python files to the sha256-pinned sdist (Octonion-Sedenion builds on it) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815339302,"data":"| numba, sparse, anywidget | 0.68.0, 0.17.0, 0.11.0 | PyPI (`RUNTIME_PINS`; runtime dependencies of quaternionic, clifford and kingdon) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815342025,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815344392,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815346715,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815348863,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815351113,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815353281,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815355603,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815357886,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815360145,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81536479,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815367081,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815369349,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815371665,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815373873,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815376176,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815378408,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815380705,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815382983,"data":"- An entry whose output a CI gate recompiles runs with `push --ci-env` on a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815385298,"data":"  CPU or GPU machine, using CPU Aer either way. The kernel then builds CI's Python 3.14.7 with CI's pins\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815387666,"data":"  through `ci/install_pins.sh` and runs the entry under it, because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815389948,"data":"  image's Python 3.13 and numpy 2.1.3 change compiled depths and durations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815392257,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81539439,"data":"## Aer on the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815396599,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815398764,"data":"- **Requesting a GPU.** Push with `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4` and a `--timeout`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815401128,"data":"  sized to the work; kaggle_run.py refuses an accelerator push without one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815403419,"data":"  The kernel installs qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 0.17.2, cuquantum-cu11 24.8.0 and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815405698,"data":"  cutensor-cu11 2.2.0 and sets `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE=GPU`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815407981999996,"data":"- **cuStateVec.** `noise_simulator(..., custatevec=True)`, or\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815410364,"data":"  `GOROROBA_AER_CUSTATEVEC=1` in the entry's environment, sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815412662,"data":"  `cuStateVec_enable` on a GPU statevector or density-matrix run; `scripts/aer_gpu_probe.py\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81541499,"data":"  --workloads n21 --configurations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815417243,"data":"  cpu_statevector,gpu_statevector_unbatched,gpu_statevector_custatevec` records\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815419627,"data":"  the three paths with Aer's reported `cuStateVec_enable`. The option excludes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815421925,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`. `docs/notes/kaggle/custatevec.md` holds the library\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815424231,"data":"  chain, the T4 push command and how to read its result.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815426507,"data":"- **Pinned GPU environment.** A push with `--gpu-env` runs the entry in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815428812,"data":"  /tmp/gororoba/gpu-venv:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815431296,"data":"  - The venv runs the image's Python with the repository's pins and the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81543363,"data":"    Aer wheels in qiskit-aer's place.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81543604,"data":"  - Before the entry, gpu_env.json records each pin's installed version, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815440401000004,"data":"    owners of `qiskit_aer/__init__.py`, Aer's devices, and two seeded Bell\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815442797,"data":"    runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815444996,"data":"  - A nonempty `failures` list stops the kernel with exit 4, before the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815447276,"data":"    entry starts. Each failure names what to fix:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815449538,"data":"    - a pin that resolved to another version;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815451813,"data":"    - a CPU qiskit-aer that shares the qiskit_aer/ files;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815454095,"data":"    - a GPU that nvidia-smi does not list;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81545636,"data":"    - a Bell run that raised, ran on another device, or left cuStateVec off;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815458705,"data":"    - on a `--gpu-aer cu13` push (spec `cuda_in_venv`), a mapped CUDA library\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815460987,"data":"      other than the driver's libcuda.so from outside the venv, or no mapped\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815463275,"data":"      CUDA library at all.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815465495,"data":"  - `push --gpu-env-with torch` adds torch 2.14.1, the build host's version,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815467787,"data":"    to the venv's pins, so a torch entry runs over the repository's numpy\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815470087,"data":"    and qiskit instead of the image's; the preflight requires it at that\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815472382,"data":"    version like every other pin.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815474612,"data":"  - Under `--gpu-aer cu13` the Aer wheel comes from an attached dataset:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815476899,"data":"    gpu_env.json's `wheel` names the file found under /kaggle/input and its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815479219,"data":"    sha256, and a missing or different file is a failure before any install.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815481522,"data":"    The report's `controller_wrappers` and `cuda_libraries` show where each\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815483814,"data":"    CUDA library resolved.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815486018,"data":"  - Read gpu-env-report.txt and install-pins.txt in the output for the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815488315,"data":"    commands' own output.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815490513,"data":"  - \"Keeping the run on the GPU\" in `docs/notes/kaggle/custatevec.md` maps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815492945,"data":"    each route to the CPU to the check that closes it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81549773,"data":"- **Using it in an entry.** The entry passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.8155001,"data":"  `calibration_snapshot.aer_device()` to `noise_simulator(snapshot, device,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815502375,"data":"  method=...)`. On a GPU the simulator batches shots of circuits of at most\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815504737,"data":"  10 active qubits without control flow and runs feed-forward circuits shot\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815507501,"data":"  by shot (`calibration_snapshot.SnapshotSimulator`).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815509786,"data":"- **Noise model width.** Restricting the snapshot and the circuit to the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81551236,"data":"  active qubits (`snapshot_laws.restrict` and `restrict_circuit`) keeps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815516818,"data":"  Aer's noise model at the circuit's width on either device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815519417,"data":"- **What the GPU is for.** It pays for density matrices at\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815521817,"data":"  `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` (11) qubits or more and for wide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815524205,"data":"  statevectors. Small dynamic circuits sample faster on the host CPUs. On\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815527242,"data":"  the 7-qubit N=21 order-finding circuits, statevector trajectories took 2.8\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815530147,"data":"  and 36 ms per shot on the CPU, against 21.7 and 54.6 ms on one T4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815532566,"data":"- **Batched shots.** `noise_simulator(..., batched_shots=True)` enables Aer's\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815534981,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`, which aborts on any circuit with control flow\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815537345,"data":"  (`if_else` lowers to `jump`), so only static circuits may batch. Batched\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81553972,"data":"  static runs are unmeasured here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815542085,"data":"- **Replay.** A GPU's seeded counts differ from the CPU's. Its records are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815544378,"data":"  replayed from their retained counts, never by resampling on CI.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815546742,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815548951,"data":"The measurements are in `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`, from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.815551293,"data":"`results/kaggle/2026-10-16T204620Z-gororoba-aer-gpu-probe`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":44.81555444,"data":"\n"}
